        {
          "title": "Whole Numbers",
          "body": "1.1 Place value and total value\nA digit's place value depends on its position. In 583,241, the 5 represents 500,000, the 8 represents\n80,000, the 3 represents 3,000, the 2 represents 200, the 4 represents 40 and the 1 represents 1.\nExpanded form: 500,000 + 80,000 + 3,000 + 200 + 40 + 1.\n\n1.2 Ordering and rounding\nTo round, inspect the digit immediately to the right of the place requested. If it is 5 or more, increase\nthe rounding digit by one; otherwise leave it unchanged."
        }
